--- !u!114 &290313417675675653
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7662925922052656418}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 96e8fe82494949145be3e0c8c1254ca7, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GuidePanelsManager
  categoriesPanel: {fileID: 1480997158745556973}
  closeEntireGuideBtn: {fileID: 355705761345998220}
  pagedGuidePanel: {fileID: 7839589709365860477}
  titleText: {fileID: 2952450899001259377}
  explanationText: {fileID: 2383680439850449829}
  pageNumberText: {fileID: 9163745368131977045}
  previousBtn: {fileID: 2442435524195253454}
  nextBtn: {fileID: 4112891113186721323}
  backToCategoriesBtn: {fileID: 594740682763871230}
  guideEntries:
  - category: 0
    pages:
    - title: COMMANDING THE SWARM
      explanationText: "Movement and control are essential for survival.\n\n\nTo
        do this, you must first select a unit by left-clicking on it:\n- In the game
        world.\n- On its portrait in the user interface.\n- Using the hotkeys ONE
        through NINE.\n\nAfter selecting a unit, right-click on an empty spot to
        order it \nto move there."
    - title: ADVANCED MOVEMENT
      explanationText: "To improve your multitasking, you can move the Conductor
        independently using \u201DWSAD\u201D.\n\nQuickly activate its Detachment
        ability by pressing \u201CE\u201D. \n\nTo go back to your puppet's body just
        press \"E\" again.\n\nRemember that when spider moves out of the screen boundaries
        (either in puppet body or on its own) the game instantly ends!"
  - category: 1
    pages:
    - title: INTERACTIONS AND COMBAT
      explanationText: "The tunnels hide valuable minerals and dangerous threats!
        \n\nTo interact with them, simply select your unit and right-click \non the
        target.\n\nYour units will automatically perform the appropriate action:
        \nThey will attack, start mining or pick up a ore."
    - title: ytrdesw
      explanationText: jegbfiwqhefo
  - category: 2
    pages:
    - title: ytrdesw
      explanationText: jegbfiwqhefo
    - title: ytrdesw
      explanationText: jegbfiwqhefo
  - category: 3
    pages:
    - title: UNIT VITALS
      explanationText: "Each robot has its own specifications and limitations. \nBe
        sure to pay close attention to them: \n\nEnergy: It depletes passively over
        time and decreases even faster during operation. If it drops to ZERO, the
        robot will shut down permanently! \n\nHealth: It is lost in combat or as
        a result of hazards. \nIf it drops to ZERO, the robot will be destroyed.
        \n\nInventory: Determines how many resources a unit can carry."
    - title: USER INTERFACE
      explanationText: "All important information is displayed on the user interface!\r\n\r\nIn
        the bottom right corner, you can see your playable characters, and their
        portraits display information such as:\r\n- LEFT GREEN BAR - HP value\r\n-
        RIGHT YELLOW BAR - Energy value\r\n- SLOTS AROUND THE PORTRAIT - number of
        inventory slots. Occupied slots turn into the color of the ore you\u2019ve
        picked up.\r\n\r\nIn the bottom-left, you\u2019ll see the same information,
        but only for the selected character, displayed as text."
    - title: SWARM CLASSES
      explanationText: "Your robotic companions are designed for specific tasks to
        optimize energy usage:\n\nMiners: Masters of excavation, use less energy
        while mining. \n\nDefenders: Built for combat, use less energy during battles.
        \n\nSpecialists: Equipped with unique abilities and usage."
  - category: 4
    pages:
    - title: THE HOLLOW CONDUCTOR
      explanationText: "Your main character cannot fight or mine directly. However,
        its special ability allows Hollow Conductor to detach from the puppet body!
        \n\nWhile detached, the Spider can perform basic actions, but you lose the
        ability to command the rest of the Swarm. \n\nYou can activate it by pressing
        \"E\"."
  - category: 5
    pages:
    - title: EVENTS
      explanationText: "When you enter the Asylum, you\u2019ll often come across
        unique events or remnants of the old world.\r\n\r\nInteract with them to
        make dialogue choices and claim reward or face the consequences!"
    - title: CRAFTING ROBOTS
      explanationText: 'Creating new robots requires the most resources.


        Once
        created, they appear with full health and energy, ready to work.


        Consider
        creating new robots when you''re low on manpower, or when your old ones can''t
        keep up and repairs would cost more than manufacturing new ones.'
    - title: CRAFTING GADGETS
      explanationText: 'Gadgets are assigned to robots to boost their base stats!


        Each
        robot can carry up to 2 gadgets, and you can remove and swap them freely
        at no additional cost.


        Consider producing them once you have a
        stable team, as producing additional workers will be more troublesome to
        maintain and manage.'
    - title: UNIT MANAGEMENT
      explanationText: "In the \u201CSwarm\u201D tab, you can manage your active
        team. \r\n\r\nHere, you can restore their health and energy, assign gadgets
        to the robots, and learn a little more about them!\r\n\r\nUsing the \u201CQuick
        Management\u201D feature allow you to quickly restore their resources in
        a single window by clicking the appropriate buttons."
    - title: DETAILED UNIT INFO
      explanationText: "In the Swarm tab, you can also click on specific unit portrait
        to review all detailed information about it.\n\nHere you will see their description,
        class, abilities, every statistic and also their assigned gadgets! \n\nOf
        course, to do that, you have to create something first, but you've already
        done that! Let's assign it!"
    - title: PATH SELECTION
      explanationText: "If you're ready, we can move on to the depths of the caves!\n\nYou\u2019ll
        often face many forks in the road, but you won\u2019t know what lies ahead!
        By using Pulsite, you can scan the branches to see what modifiers they hold.\n\nModifiers
        change the amount of resources and threats, and even have their own unique
        effects, so watch your step!"
  interactionSound:
    Guid:
      Data1: 0
      Data2: 0
      Data3: 0
      Data4: 0
    Path: 
